      "writtenOn": "2026-05-28T20:07:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Recapping chats from earlier:\n* This format of modifying the VDO makes it pretty hard to tell what\u0027s changing.\n* In spite of the [comments](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/usb_pd_vdo.h;l\u003d678;drc\u003d41520674f93769897147c5f9bb0ac191e9840379) in `usb_pd_vdo.h`, I think that it\u0027s practical to make a packed struct for the PD 3.0 IDH. You\u0027d just have to split the DFP Product Type field at the byte boundary and access it via helper functions that did bit ops on the two fields. That\u0027s annoying, but it\u0027s less annoying than doing bit ops on every field, every time we handle this VDO.",
      "revId": "2abc9c53af8c5c76933e334759b5fabdccc95f5b",
